    "updated_at": "2019-07-21T19:49:52Z",
    "body": "Additional note: if using command substitution in `PROMPT` in zsh (instead of setting it from `precmd`), you need the option `prompt_subst` to be set. Otherwise, you just get a literal `$(starship prompt --status=$?)` as your prompt, which is less-than-helpful.\r\n\r\n~~I'm have not been able to find information about any analogous option that needs to be set in bash.~~ The analogous option in bash is called `promptvars`, and is set by default.",
